---

Specimens in the `Invertebrate zoology` catalog format show the invertebrate
form. Sex and life stage work the same way across taxon groups; see
[Measurements](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/).

{% aside type="caution" %}

Invertebrate zoology support is in beta. Check exports against your collection's
requirements before relying on them.

{% /aside %}

## Measurements

The `Ecological interactions` section is visible by default. Turn on
`Show specimen morphometrics` to reveal the measurement fields; saved
morphometric values automatically reopen this section when the record is loaded.

- `Sex`: select from the configured specimen-sex controlled vocabulary.
- `Life stage`: select from the configured life-stage controlled vocabulary.
- `Caste`: social-insect caste, when applicable (`drone`, `gyne`, `king`,
  `major`, `minor`, `queen`, `reproductive`, `soldier`, or `worker`).
- `Ecological interactions`: `Host organism` and `Host part`.
- `Specimen morphometrics` (optional): `Head width (mm)`, `Body length (mm)`,
  `Upper wingspan (mm)`, and `Lower wingspan (mm)`.
- `Remarks`: additional ecological or specimen notes.

## Environmental conditions

Environmental conditions are recorded on sites and collection events rather than
on individual specimens:

- Record `Canopy cover` on the site under `Site Attributes`.
- Record temperature, humidity, pH, dissolved oxygen, and flow velocity on the
  collecting event under [environmental data](/en/usages/events/).

## Parts and symbionts

Invertebrate catalogs include the `Specimen Parts` tab and `Associated Data`
tab, but do not currently include symbiont-detection fields or the symbiont tab
(symbionts are available in `Mammalogy`, `Ornithology`, `Herpetology`, and
`Ichthyology`). Record host associations for an invertebrate specimen under
`Ecological interactions` above. See
[Specimen Parts](/en/usages/specimens/parts/) and
[Symbionts](/en/usages/specimens/symbionts/).
